Use the portable /usr/bin/env bash interpreter for the two upstream
ctest drivers.

tests/extract.sh and tests/clean.sh are registered directly as ctest
commands, so CTest execve()s them through their shebang.  On HarmonyOS
bash does not live at /bin/bash (it is /data/service/hnp/bin/bash, which
the CI profile puts on PATH), so execve fails with ENOENT and every case
is reported as "Process not started ... [no such file or directory]"
with a BAD_COMMAND verdict -- 0/14 cases actually run.

Resolving bash through PATH keeps the scripts portable and lets the HNP
bash from the build profile be used.  Only the interpreter line changes;
no test logic and no .expect file is touched.
--- a/tests/extract.sh
+++ b/tests/extract.sh
@@ -1,4 +1,4 @@
-#!/bin/bash
+#!/usr/bin/env bash
 set -e
 set -o pipefail
 
--- a/tests/clean.sh
+++ b/tests/clean.sh
@@ -1,4 +1,4 @@
-#!/bin/bash
+#!/usr/bin/env bash
 set -e
 set -o pipefail
 
